# Normalise line endings so a checkout is byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true holds CRLF while the
# repository holds LF. Anything that hashes or diffs the working tree then gets
# a different answer depending on the operating system — which is exactly how
# the asset stamp came to differ between a Windows build and the Linux CI
# runner. Forcing LF in the working tree removes the class of problem rather
# than papering over one instance of it.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
